## Sustained lifecycle regression

PR #783 adds `mutation_sustained_replacements_append_and_compaction_reopen_each_round`.

The test starts with 32 immutable append segments, then executes four rounds of:

1. replace one visible physical version and append one new logical ID;
2. publish through `prepare_delta`;
3. reopen and run bounded same-level compaction;
4. reopen again and verify document count plus replacement/append hydration.

The full `hawdb-search` library suite now passes **711 tests** (19 ignored), with the mutation subset at **26 passed**. The test is a finite lifecycle witness; sustained production RSS and power-loss qualification remain open.
